    "body": "Turns out https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/32092 was incomplete and the issue can still happen:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/actions/runs/39809026827/job/119929911875#step:14:14454\r\n\r\nThe basic idea is that peer1 disconnects to clear its orphan state. This happens in `DisconnectNodes`->`DeleteNode`->`FinalizeNode`->`TxDownloadManager::DisconnectedPeer`.\r\n\r\nIn my prior fix, I assumed that `DisconnectNodes` in the `net` thread would be possible to sync on via a ping-pong. However, the msghand thread may hold a reference to the node, preventing deletion and only moving the node to `m_nodes_disconnected`. Afterward, the `net` thread may hand the pings to the `msghand` thread and go to sleep for a bit.\r\n\r\nThus, the test proceed and cause a split `getdata`, meaning that `peer2.wait_for_parent_requests([int(parent_peekaboo_AB[\"txid\"], 16), int(parent_missing[\"txid\"], 16)])` fails.\r\n\r\nFix this by just waiting for `TxDownloadManager::DisconnectedPeer` to have happened via `self.wait_until(lambda: len(node.getorphantxs(verbosity=2)[0][\"from\"]) == 1)`.\r\n\r\n\r\nEdit: Possible diff to reproduce with ~10% failure rate:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/src/net.cpp b/src/net.cpp\r\nindex 1201d3bcb4..e81623484b 100644\r\n--- a/src/net.cpp\r\n+++ b/src/net.cpp\r\n@@ -2229,2 +2229,3 @@ void CConnman::SocketHandlerConnected(const std::vector<CNode*>& nodes,\r\n                     WakeMessageHandler();\r\n+            UninterruptibleSleep(333ms *m_nodes_disconnected.size());\r\n                 }\r\n@@ -3261,2 +3262,3 @@ void CConnman::ThreadMessageHandler()\r\n             }\r\n+            UninterruptibleSleep(33ms);\r\n         }\r\n```\r\n\r\nCmd: `./bld-cmake/test/functional/test_runner.py $(for i in {1..20}; do echo -n \"p2p_orphan_handling.py \";done) -j $( nproc )`\r\n",
